@ref Dieu 143 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:259-286; src:law139-2025-qh15:333-339)
`an unqualified ancillary provider` MEANS `An act in insurance business` WITH
    `is insurance, reinsurance, ceding or brokerage business` IS FALSE
    `is done without a licence to establish and operate` IS FALSE
    `is done outside the scope of the licence` IS FALSE
    `is insurance agency activity` IS FALSE
    `is an ancillary insurance service` IS TRUE
    `the actor does not meet the conditions of law to do it` IS TRUE
    `is colluding with a beneficiary to settle a claim unlawfully` IS FALSE
    `is forging documents or deliberately falsifying information in a claim dossier` IS FALSE
    `is forging documents or deliberately falsifying information to refuse a claim after the insured event` IS FALSE
    `is causing loss to one's own property or health to get insurance benefits` IS FALSE
    `is threatening or coercing the making of an insurance contract` IS FALSE
`an adviser with no degree` MEANS `A provider of ancillary services (conditions)` WITH
    `is an individual giving advice` IS TRUE
    `has full civil act capacity` IS TRUE
    `has a degree in insurance` IS FALSE
    `has a degree in another field and an ancillary insurance certificate for advice` IS FALSE
    `is an organisation with legal personality, lawfully established and operating` IS FALSE
    `its staff directly doing ancillary work have full capacity and suitable degrees or certificates` IS FALSE
